//
// Doc 31 R1, the host-only half: ffn_resident's addressing arithmetic,
// emulated to exactness.
//
// The resident FFN interior moves every byte through hand-derived patterns
// (the w_up packing, the shim's row-major->blocked retile, the strided
// chunk extraction, the w_down slices, a global K order assembled from
// three herds' loops). builders/test_ffn_resident.py emulates the device's
// exact address arithmetic in numpy, f64 throughout, and requires the
// composition to equal gelu(hidden @ w_up) @ w_down EXACTLY -- so only
// ordering and addressing are tested, and a slip in either cannot hide
// behind a tolerance.
//
// This arm is deliberately the one that stays LIVE while the operator's
// device gate (run_npu2_ffn_resident_peano.lit) is parked on the
// air-fuse-channels crash: no aircc, no XRT, no kernel objects, no NPU.
//
// No framework dependency (pytest is not in the sandbox venv): the file
// runs as a plain script and prints a named pass count, matched exactly so
// a check that stops being collected fails here rather than passing
// quietly.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/builders/test_ffn_resident.py | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: ffn_resident emulation tests: 5/5 passed
